15 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Diagram showing analysis of CRC-infiltrating gamma-delta T cells. Panel a illustrates data collection from single-cell RNA sequencing of colorectal cancer tissues, focusing on gamma-delta T cell markers. Panel b features a UMAP visualization, distinguishing cell types by color, and a pie chart showing composition percentages: TRM at 59.05%, Teff at 26.17%, Tex at 11.96%, and Tpex at 2.83%. Panel c presents a heatmap of normalized AUC scores across different gene markers and subsets. Panel d displays a bar graph comparing activation and exhaustion scores for TRM, Teff, and Tex subsets.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt <> /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (A composite image with three sections: \(a\) A pie chart showing 30,025 predicted TF-target pairs; 56% have a source, 44% do not. \(b\) A schematic depicting TF-target prediction using SCENIC, ChIP-seq TF peak identification, and data from the ChIP-Atlas. \(c\) Four scatter plots showing regulon specificity scores \(RSS\) for TRM, Teff, Tex, and Tpex cell types, highlighting key transcription factors.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (UMAP plots showing simulated cell identity shifts for TRM-specific and Teff-specific vectors. Each plot illustrates the impact of different gene knockouts \(NR3C1, ELF1, FOXO1, IKZF1, FOSL2 for TRM-specific; XBP1, IRF1, BHLHE40, KLF2, ATF3 for Teff-specific\) on cell distribution. Cells are colored in green and blue, representing Teff and TRM, respectively, with arrows indicating shift directions. Axes labeled UMAP1 and UMAP2.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Volcano plot comparing Teff and TRM, depicting gene expression differences with Log2 Fold Change on the x-axis and -Log10\(adjusted P-value\) on the y-axis. Significant genes are orange, insignificant are blue. T cell function-related genes and inferred ligand targets are highlighted. Inset lists the top 15 ligands affecting TRM to effector transition with activity levels next to each. Bottom graph shows ligand target gene expression in gamma-delta T cells, with bubble size and color indicating percent and average expression, respectively.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (A composite of three figures analyzing gene expression. Panel \(a\) is a volcano plot of Tex versus Teff, showing gene significance based on fold change. Blue dots represent insignificant genes, and orange dots signify significant ones, with labeled genes highlighted. Panel \(b\) lists the top 15 inferred ligands affecting effector exhaustion with associated activity scores. Panel \(c\) is a dot plot showing the inferred top ligands' target gene expression in exhausted gamma delta T cells, with color and size indicating average expression and percentage, respectively.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Heatmap visualizing phenotype-shifting ligand enrichment in epithelial \(left\) and immune cell types \(right\). Color intensity indicates normalized AUC values across subsets, using a blue to red gradient. Epithelial types include MSI-H and MSS variations; immune types include plasma B, pDC, neutrophils, fibroblasts, and others. The columns compare TRM2Teff and Teff2Tex transitions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Scatter plot labeled \215TRM-like to effectors\216 with cosine shift on the x-axis and negative log10 FDR on the y-axis. Red and blue dots represent significant genes, with labels for genes like KLRK1 and CCL3. Non-significant genes are black dots. A red line indicates the shift threshold. To the right, a list shows top 15 NicheNet-inferred ligands with corresponding activity values, including TGFB1 and IL15. Blue and red boxes denote differentially and not differentially expressed genes in effectors. Legends clarify dot colors and threshold lines.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
